{
  "id": "unique-paths",
  "order": 37,
  "title": "Unique Paths",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "pattern": "Grid DP",
  "statement": "A robot starts at the top-left of an `m x n` grid and can only move right or down. Return the number of distinct paths to the bottom-right corner.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= m, n <= 100",
    "The answer fits in a 32-bit signed integer for the tested sizes"
  ],
  "function": {
    "name": "uniquePaths",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "m",
        "type": "int"
      },
      {
        "name": "n",
        "type": "int"
      }
    ],
    "returns": "int"
  },
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(m * n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "hints": [
    "How many ways reach a cell? It depends on two neighbours.",
    "paths(r, c) = paths(r-1, c) + paths(r, c-1), with the first row and column all 1.",
    "Use a single row array updated in place: row[j] += row[j-1]. (Combinatorics: C(m+n-2, m-1).)"
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
